cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use zmz in your work, please cite it."
title: "zmz: Mass Spectrometry Open Data Format Library for Zig"
type: software
abstract: "zmz is a Zig library for mass-spectrometry data, starting with mzML. It streams files in flat memory, looks records up by ID or position, decodes and encodes binary arrays (zlib and MS-Numpress), writes plain and indexed mzML, and resolves PSI-MS and Unit Ontology terms."
version: 0.1.0
url: "https://github.com/eneskemalergin/zmz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eneskemalergin/zmz"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ergin"
    given-names: "Enes K."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9810-7399"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - mass-spectrometry
  - proteomics
  - mzml
  - zig
  - data-format
  - parser
